<section class="eg-section" id="audit-example"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">A fictional campaign review</p><h2>A missed callback needs an owner.</h2><p>A team reports four checks in place, cannot confirm when contact data was checked and knows its callbacks lack owners and dates.</p></div><div class="eg-grid"><article class="eg-card"><h3>What the answers establish</h3><p>One reported gap: follow-up ownership. One unresolved check: contact data. The answers alone do not establish why bookings are low.</p><p><strong>Result:</strong> start with the reported gap, then verify the missing information.</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>What to do first</h3><ol class="eg-steps"><li>Assign open callbacks to a person, with a due date and the buyer’s reason.</li><li>Check a current contact sample for changed roles and unusable numbers.</li></ol><p>Use the records you find to decide whether a wider change is needed.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="eg-section eg-paper" id="audit-method"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">Transparent rules</p><h2>Know how the priorities are chosen.</h2></div><div class="eg-grid eg-three"><article class="eg-card"><h3>Known gaps come first.</h3><p>A No answer produces an action for that specific check. The tool puts these before unresolved checks and shows up to three initial actions.</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Missing evidence stays open.</h3><p>Not sure produces a verification task. All six answers remain visible, even when only three actions are prioritised. Within each group, checks follow their order above.</p></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Six Yes answers need validation.</h3><p>The tool reports that your answers flagged no gaps. Confirm the controls against actual records. It does not grade your team or predict campaign performance.</p></article></div><p class="eg-small">This tool does not listen to calls, inspect data quality, test email delivery or compare your results against an industry benchmark.</p></div></section>
<section class="eg-section" id="audit-next"><div class="eg-wrap"><div class="eg-heading"><p class="eg-kicker">Choose the next investigation</p><h2>Take the finding to the right resource.</h2></div><div class="eg-grid eg-three"><article class="eg-card"><h3>Review the measurement.</h3><p>Check the definitions and records behind account coverage, conversations and follow-up.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/articles/cold-calling-metrics-campaign-quality/">Read the campaign metrics guide →</a></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Inspect your opening.</h3><p>Use the separate rule-based checker to review the words in your cold call opening.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/cold-call-script-checker/">Check Your Cold Call Script →</a></article><article class="eg-card"><h3>Follow the booked meetings.</h3><p>Examine attendance, sales acceptance and opportunities for one group of bookings.</p><a class="eg-link" href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">Check My Meeting Results →</a></article></div></div></section>
